opencode2-bin packages the OpenCode 2.0 release line, an open source AI
coding agent for the terminal.

This package ships the self-contained binary built by upstream and
installs it as `opencode2`, so it can coexist with the v1
`opencode-bin` package (which provides `opencode`). Upstream publishes
the 2.0 line only to the npm registry as `@opencode/cli-linux-x64`;
there is no GitHub release tarball for it, so this package repacks
that npm artifact.

The binary is compiled with Bun and is self-contained (no runtime
dependencies). The default build targets glibc x86_64 with AVX2. On a
CPU without AVX2, use the `-baseline` variant instead.

OpenCode v1 and v2 share the same configuration and state directories
(`~/.config/opencode`, `~/.local/share/opencode`). To test 2.0 without
touching the v1 state, run it with an isolated XDG environment, e.g.:

  XDG_CONFIG_HOME=~/.config/opencode2 \
  XDG_DATA_HOME=~/.local/share/opencode2 \
  opencode2

Homepage: https://opencode.ai
